      "math_academy_id": "e-9210",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n\nLet $Y=\\dfrac12X^2.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $a$ | $b$ | $18$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.1$ | $c$ | $d$ | $0.4$ |\n\nFind the values of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y = \\dfrac12X^2$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $8$ | $18$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $8$ | $18$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n\nHence, $a=2, b=8, c=0.2,$ and $d=0.3.$",
